  "reasoning": [
    "A cell is low <= value < low + width on each axis, low being the stored value minus half the width for 1 to 31 bits (lnk_02). c17-rl's 16-bit cell runs latitude [386072576, 386138112) and longitude [-903675904, -903610368).",
    "c17-rl's 32-bit fix sits exactly on that cell's south-west corner, (386072576, -903675904): low <= value on both axes, so the cell holds it. Its 32-bit cell [value, value + 1) lies inside the 16-bit cell, so the two overlap: stationary. The 16-bit cell holds a finer position and adds nothing: the box is the fix's own cell rl_32, merged false, precision_bits 32, centre half a unit north and east of the stored value.",
    "Kept with 3 packets at 2791.128 m. Medians over the counted receipts: SNR 5, 6 and 7 dB give 6.0; RSSI -90, -95 and -100 dBm give -95.0 (lnk_04, percentile_cont).",
    "position_uncertainty_m is the larger half-width of each end's box, rl_32 0.005550 m plus g16 363.750397 m, = 363.755947 m (lnk_05).",
    "c17-ru's 16-bit cell runs longitude [-903675904, -903610368); its 32-bit fix has longitude_i -903610368, exactly the upper edge, and the cell's centre latitude. The value is not < low + width, so the cell does not hold it; the fix's cell [-903610368, -903610367) only touches the 16-bit cell, so they do not overlap.",
    "The stored coordinates are 285.485 m apart (half the cell's east-west width), beyond the 40 m floor: c17-ru has moved, has no position within 30 minutes of its receipts, and each is dropped by lnk_02."
  ],
